    "summary": "With daemon threads enabled, the main thread no longer builds its handler runtime at boot: lazyForward (src/daemon/threads/lazy-runtime.ts) builds buildHandlerRuntime, the in-daemon client and installStepDaemonClient on the first request the router keeps local, logs 'handler runtime built on the main thread', answers a failed build with its error and retries on the next request; shutdown stops understanding routes only if built. With threads disabled the runtime is built at boot as before. The daemon-level proof that routed requests leave it unbuilt is t6.",
